 "stop": "3 quatrains",
 "poem": "Or a lingering heave of sorrow,\nOr the feathery touch away\nOf a long-lost daughter's finger,\nAnd the way that sweetly they\nWandered on the moonlight skies, together\nIn the river shadow.\nNow the woodlands are full again,\nWith the blossoms underfoot; below,\nA bough is tinged with bright crimson\nFor a time when summer is away\nFrom its starry heaven of\nPallid mists. A maiden",
